{"task":"transcribe","language":"en","duration":72.19225,"text":"This is how I run my 37 AI agent team to handle my business. Everything starts with this conductor agent here, which I'm running Claude code headless. I can paste anything I want in here and it'll start delegating tasks to the other agents through something called paperclip. This was an open source repo that allows you to run as many agents as you want. You see here at my conductor, commanding all of the other department heads on what to do and the specific task I gave it. And you also see I have Fable 5 running as the agent for my Claude code headless instance. And all of this is able to connect to Hermes, which right now I have running GLM 5.2. You see Hermes is the action layer between what I want and what the tasks are that get done. Claude code, since I wanted to use my subscription and not the API, I have to use in headless. And we all know we want Fable telling the other agents what to do. And the most important part is the brain that all the agents pull from. Since I have two companies, multiple business partners and multiple employees, it's really easy for everything to be in here so none of the agents hallucinate. And it helps me stay so much more organized. And the best part is I'm running all of this on my Mac mini completely locally. I have connected to Tailscale and I'm running it as a web app on my actual MacBook. So I can go anywhere in the world and it's always gonna be running. And if you want the free repo to try out for yourself, just come and build and I'll send it over.","words":null,"segments":[{"avg_logprob":-0.13614535409640643,"compression_ratio":1.7370030581039755,"end":3.64,"id":1,"no_speech_prob":0.05033370107412338,"seek":0,"start":0.0,"temperature":0.0,"text":" This is how I run my 37 AI agent team to handle my business.","tokens":[50364,639,307,577,286,1190,452,13435,7318,9461,1469,281,4813,452,1606,13,50546],"words":null},{"avg_logprob":-0.13614535409640643,"compression